[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Am I All Right?]
[00:14.75]Why did Mr. Gilbert telephone Dr. Millington?
[00:22.07]While John Gilbert was in hospital,
[00:25.79]he asked his doctor to tell him whether his operation had been successful,
[00:32.63]but the doctor refused to do so.
[00:37.27]The following day, the patient asked for a bedside telephone.
[00:43.78]When he was alone, he telephoned the hospital exchange and asked for Doctor Millington.
[00:52.88]When the doctor answered the phone,
[00:55.78]Mr. Gilbert said he was inquiring about a certain patient,
[01:01.13]a Mr. John Gilbert.
[01:04.22]He asked if Mr. Gilbert's operation had been successful
[01:08.58]and the doctor told him that it had been.
[01:12.39]He then asked when Mr. Gilbert would be allowed to go home
[01:17.31]and the doctor told him that he would have to stay in hosptial for another two weeks.
[01:24.28]Then Dr. Millington asked the caller if he was a relative of the patient.
[01:30.61]'No,' the patient answered,
[01:33.52]'I am Mr. John Gilbert.  '
